{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Economically distinct benefits in a combined offer can be identified separately; this is an interpretive modeling choice for applying 'any gifts' and the fee/charge discount exception.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"A component is classified as a gift only after examining its terms and economic substance. Paragraph 9's 'may be considered a gift' does not establish that every additional return or incentive is a gift.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The fee/charge discount exception applies to the component that is itself such a discount, rather than to all benefits packaged with it.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The phrase 'should not offer' is represented as a prohibition under this selected Code of Conduct restriction; the result does not determine criminal liability or compliance with other requirements.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"c110b7c8b6506e151958dd008461e5225ee74e977445e7ae3cf59f7fafa3aeae","candidate_id":"candidate.8fede9ef89084ceba11540db0199e293","controlled_language":"[TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED] Within scope, the result answers whether offering this component is prohibited by the selected gift restriction: true means the component is a gift, is not a discount of fees or charges, and promotes a specific investment product or is linked to a particular type of investment product. False means this component does not meet that conjunction; it does not establish that the combined offer is compliant or legally approved. An unknown classification or promotional connection remains unknown unless the other facts logically determine the result.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["scope"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":["issue.7639c02211284eaa8cdd84bfd9ad810e","issue.1a83656495c2416d8c183bb6271ea8c3","issue.933bcdfec17641c4a253d6e1af7a8c35","issue.ed77d018edac472f80a9aea98ba4fd00"],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"A single offer-level Boolean such as 'includes a discount' would hide the difference between an excepted fee discount and a separate potentially prohibited gift. A Boolean limited to promotion of a named fund would also omit product-type promotion, including funds from particular fund houses. Finally, absence of structured-product classification does not remove the need to classify the component under the gift restriction.","run_id":"run.5536e2694ccd404aa5c8cf55fdd1443e","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"9cc272f84dbcec164f1a7a7a567859d8a6feb7fc34af22d7bef3e7688f64f736","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987","db43e253bea18.u7.1360"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Application of the paragraph 10 gift restriction to an individual component of a promotional offer"}